# Waveger — required environment variables.
#
# Do not fill this in by hand and rename it. Every value below is injected by
# Vercel and pulled down (ADR 0008):
#
#     vercel env pull .env.local
#
# `scripts/setup.sh` walks a new machine through that and everything around it.
# This file exists to document what has to be present, and what each one is
# for, not to be a template you copy.

# ── Postgres (Neon, London, via the Vercel Marketplace) ───────────────────
# Both are set by the integration. Getting them the wrong way round fails
# intermittently under load rather than immediately, which is why the code
# names them explicitly rather than reading one "database URL".

# Pooled (`-pooler` host). What the API uses: every query runs in a serverless
# function, so the pooler does the connection management.
DATABASE_URL=

# Direct. What migrations and the test harness use. Session state — the
# `search_path` per-test isolation depends on — does not survive the pooler.
DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED=

# ── Chart ingestion (ADR 0002) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Not read by any code yet; the Apify actor arrives with chart ingestion.
# Set on the Vercel project like everything else, so a pull restores it.
# Sensitive in Preview and Production; readable in Development, because
# `vercel env pull` has to be able to read the value back.
APIFY_TOKEN=

# ── Song media (Apple Music, ADR 0002) ────────────────────────────────────
# Not read by any code yet; these arrive with artwork and previews (WAV-12).
# Together they sign the MusicKit developer token — an ES256 JWT with the key
# id in its header and the team id as the issuer.
#
# The private key is the one credential here that cannot be recovered from its
# source. Apple serves the .p8 once, at creation, and deletes its copy; two
# earlier Waveger keys were revoked in August 2026 precisely because their
# downloads were lost and neither could sign anything. If Vercel's copy is
# ever lost, the key is dead and the fix is a new one, not a re-download.
APPLE_MUSIC_TEAM_ID=
APPLE_MUSIC_KEY_ID=
APPLE_MUSIC_PRIVATE_KEY=

# ── Ports, and the native app ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# None of these belong here. Each one lives in the .env of the app that reads
# it, because a file at this level is read by nothing — this one is only ever
# pulled from Vercel, and a root `.env` is neither loaded by a framework nor
# sourced by your shell. In an Orca worktree, `orca.yaml` writes them for you.
#
# apps/web/.env
#   PORT                    the web app's port. Next reads PORT before it loads
#                           any env file, so `apps/web`'s dev script sources
#                           this itself.
#
# apps/native/.env
#   RCT_METRO_PORT          the Metro port. Expo loads this file by itself.
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL     where a deployed build finds the API. Leave it
#                           unset in development and the app derives the host
#                           from the Metro server it was loaded from, so a
#                           phone on the same network reaches your machine
#                           rather than its own localhost.
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_PORT    the port to pair with that derived host — the web
#                           app's port, which worktrees move off 3000.
#
# Only `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` reaches the native bundle. Nothing secret goes there.
